import WideTrail.Hades.AutomatonCheck

/-!
# Forward-space automaton certificate for HorizenLabs BN254, width three

Data and kernel checks for the middle bound of `WideTrail.Poseidon2.BN254MiddleSharp`. The
partial-round matrix is `internalMatrix = [[2, 1, 1], [1, 2, 1], [1, 1, 3]]` of
`WideTrail.Poseidon2.BN254`, over `ZMod p` with `p = fieldModulus` (the value of
`Poseidon2.BN254.modulus`), the S-box is on coordinate `0`, and the window is the `56` partial
rounds.

* `internalRows`, `externalRows`: the internal and the external matrix of the instance file, row
  `i` holding the coefficients of output coordinate `i`. `internalDiagonal`: the diagonal
  `(1, 1, 2)` of the internal matrix written as `diag (1, 1, 2) + J` (`internalDiag`).
* `states`: a forward-space automaton (`Hades.AutomatonCheck.AState`) with `57` states. State `0`
  has no functional (it stands for every difference), potential `2` and depth `0`. For `k ≥ 1`,
  state `k` has depth `k` and stands for the differences on which its functionals vanish (one
  for odd `k`, two for even `k`): a subspace that contains every difference with which a trail
  whose first `k` rounds are inactive, inactive, active, inactive, active, … can enter round `k`.
  Its potential is `1` for odd `k` and `0` for even `k`. For the states of depth less than `56`:
  an active round leads from `0` and from every odd state to state `0`, and from an even state
  `k ≥ 2` to state `k + 1`; an inactive round leads from `0` to `1` and from an odd state `k` to
  `k + 1`, and is impossible from an even state `k ≥ 2`.
* `trailStates`, `trailSboxOutputs`: a trail through the `64` rounds of the BN254 schedule (`4`
  full rounds with the external matrix, `56` partial rounds with the internal matrix and the
  S-box at coordinate `0`, `4` full rounds): row `n` of `trailStates` is the difference entering
  round `n`, row `n` of `trailSboxOutputs` the difference after its S-box layer.
* `middleStates`, `middleOutputs`: rows `4, …, 60` of `trailStates` and coordinate `0` of rows
  `4, …, 59` of `trailSboxOutputs`, read as a trail through the `56` partial rounds.

The checks, each by `decide +kernel`:

* `automaton_check`: `Hades.AutomatonCheck.checkAll` passes for the window of `56` rounds with
  `internalRows`, the S-box at coordinate `0` and start state `0`; `start_pot`: the start state
  has potential `2`.
* `trail_check`: `Hades.AutomatonCheck.checkHadesTrail` passes for the `4 + 56 + 4` rounds;
  `trail_weight`: the charged weight of that trail is `43`.
* `middle_trail_check`: `Hades.RelationCheck.checkTrail` passes for `middleStates` and
  `middleOutputs` with `internalDiagonal`, over the `56` partial rounds.

The data were computed outside Lean from the literals of the instance files; nothing depends on
how they were found, since the checks are complete. This file imports only
`WideTrail.Hades.AutomatonCheck`, which imports only `WideTrail.Hades.RelationCheck` and through
it `Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic`.

## What is not claimed

The checks are statements about lists of natural numbers. What they mean for trails is proved in
`WideTrail.Hades.Automaton` and `WideTrail.Hades.WindowRelation`, and applied in
`WideTrail.Poseidon2.BN254MiddleSharp` and `WideTrail.Poseidon2.Checks.BN254MiddleSharp`. The
witness trail is a trail in the `IsTrail` model (supports, masks and linear maps only); it is
not claimed to be realised by an input pair or a key.
-/

